Hi Team,

I’m currently working on a new Power BI solution for our Manhattan sites focused on Discontinued, NPI 180, and NPI 360 SKUs, with the goal of giving teams better visibility into how inventory and slotting are being managed across the SKU lifecycle.

One of the first things that stood out in the data is the work the IQC teams have already done around discontinued SKUs. Nearly all discontinued SKUs in the current population are no longer slotted, which is a strong indication that active pick space is being protected as items move out of the network.

As we look beyond that, the data is also beginning to surface a few areas where the BI can help drive action. We are seeing discontinued inventory that still has BOH after being removed from active slots, along with NPI 180 and NPI 360 SKUs that have inventory on hand but are not currently slotted. These are opportunities to better understand inventory disposition, slot readiness, and how effectively we are managing SKUs as they move from new item introduction through discontinuation.

The intent of this BI is not just to provide visibility, but to help identify where attention may be needed and make it easier for the teams to move from insight to action.

I’d appreciate any additional observations or use cases the IQC team would like us to consider as we continue developing the report.